      },
      "exhibit": {
        "slug": "skulloflarsmoller",
        "inv": 4,
        "title": "Skull of Lars Møller",
        "medium": "",
        "description": "Meet  Lars, a guy who lost a very heated argument during the Battle of Visby on July 27, 1361. While the Danish army was busy sorting out the local Gutnic peasants, Lars caught a severe case of an axe to the head, leaving a deeply memorable impression on his skull.\nTo top it all off, one of his eyes miraculously turned into something resembling pure amber over the centuries, which conservators managed to lovingly stabilize.",
        "tags": [],
        "gallery": [
          "92fd36086931",
          "f8a6bb0d310d"
        ],
        "plaque": true
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "dscf2869",
      "media": "f1661f4f6c80",
      "x": -351.65,
      "y": 902.17,
      "w": 238.56,
      "rotation": 0,
      "plaqueAt": {
        "dx": 15.5,
        "dy": 8.1
      },
      "on": "cabinet",
      "exhibit": {
        "slug": "mockupofdavid",
        "inv": 6,
        "title": "Mockup of David",
        "medium": "",
        "description": "Before tackling his famous 17-foot masterpiece, Michelangelo carved this smaller scale model just to make sure he could nail the nose. Think of it as a rough draft, only chiseled out of top-shelf Italian marble instead of sketched on paper.\n\nMysteriously lost for centuries, the head resurfaced a few years ago and was promptly snapped up by a private collector. Experts consider its value \"priceless,\" which in the art world is speak for a number that makes even billionaires break into a cold sweat.",
        "tags": [],
        "gallery": [],
        "plaque": true
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "dscf2765",
      "media": "9814ae499102",
      "x": 222.15,
      "y": 969.82,
      "w": 140.35,
      "rotation": 0,
      "plaqueAt": {
        "dx": 4.4,
        "dy": 15.7
      },
      "on": "cabinet",
      "exhibit": {
        "slug": "mysteriousidol",
        "inv": 2,
        "title": "Mysterious Idol",
        "medium": "",
        "description": "Measuring just 21 centimeters tall, this figurine of a winged, tentacled creature bears the word \"Cthulhu\" and several strange symbols carved into its side. Nobody has a clue what the name means, and the script remains completely undeciphered to this day.\n\nThe real puzzle, however, isn't the unknown language, but the fact that the idol is constantly wet for completely unexplained reasons. Experts have already tried dehumidifiers, hair dryers, and lab tests, yet the stone stubbornly keeps seeping water, as if it were just pulled from the ocean floor.",
        "tags": [],
        "gallery": [],
        "plaque": true
      }
