        "title": "The King in Yellow",
        "medium": "",
        "description": "Standing an impressive 45 centimeters tall, this statue depicts a figure draped in a bright yellow robe, using a tentacle to remove a white wooden mask from where its face should be. The catch is that there is no face underneath at all. To this day, scientists are fiercely debating the artifact's true meaning and original purpose.\n\nThe only certainty is that the piece has a rather peculiar effect on anyone who gets too close. Those who stare at it for too long suddenly start rambling about a mysterious \"yellow sign\" and promptly lose their grip on sanity.",
