        "inv": 5,
        "title": "The Lost Arch found",
        "medium": "",
        "description": "This front page of The Egyptian Gazette from August 4, 1936, breaks a story that would make even Moses drop his tablets. Under the bold headline \"Lost Ark Discovered,\" the world first learned that famous American archaeologist Indiana Jones had actually tracked down the legendary biblical Ark of the Covenant, apparently using his usual blend of academic brilliance, a bullwhip, and a total disregard for basic safety protocols.\n\nThe find of the century sparked an instant global sensation, though as is often the case with ancient souvenirs, the celebration didn't last long. If you decide to lean in for a closer look at this rare newspaper, you might want to keep your eyes tightly shut just in case something flies out and melts your face off.",
